  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Problem Statement\n\nYou are given an array A of size N.\n\nYou may perform right-rotation any number of times:\n\n1 right rotation: last element moves to front\n\n\nYour task:\n\n✔ Determine the minimum number of right rotations needed to make the array strictly increasing.\n\nIf it is not possible, return -1.\n\nExample\n\nInput:\n\n5\n3 4 5 1 2\n\n\nRight rotation once:\n\n2 3 4 5 1 → not sorted\n\n\nRight rotation twice:\n\n1 2 3 4 5 → sorted ✔\n\n\nOutput:\n\n2",
    "constraints": [
      "nil"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Integer  n- array size\nN values of Array",
    "outputFormat": "array of Integers",
    "notes": [],
